unty","/arc-plc/new-jersey/burlington-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids August to September came in under 90% of normal in 35 of those 75 years. In 2025 that same pair landed at 50% of normal on the middle, and January to February was 52%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 59% and March to April at 61% on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 1965, with grid 23622 at 63% that year.</p>"}
